A script hook runs with `BOOPING_ARTIFACT`, `BOOPING_INSTANCE` and `BOOPING_WORKDIR` in its
environment and with the workdir as its cwd. The fixture script writes all four out, so the sandbox
paths normalize to `{CWD}` in the expected file. On a machine with no `{instance}` in its artifact
path `BOOPING_INSTANCE` is empty.

-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-hooks
title: Hooks
summary: Hook-bearing fixture for playbook-transition.
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/playbook.yaml --
state: main
graph:
  only: []

states:
  main:
    artifact: index.md
    initial: intaking
    statuses:
      intaking:
        transitions:
          - to: noted
            when: the environment is recorded
            hooks: ["script env-note"]
      noted: {terminal: true}
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/only/prompt.md --
---
summary: Only step.
---

Only body.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/_scripts/env-note --
#!/bin/sh
{
  echo "artifact=$BOOPING_ARTIFACT"
  echo "instance=$BOOPING_INSTANCE"
  echo "workdir=$BOOPING_WORKDIR"
  echo "cwd=$(pwd)"
} > "$BOOPING_WORKDIR/env.txt"
-- fixtures/cwd/run/.keep --
-- cmd --
chmod +x ../home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/_scripts/env-note
booping playbook-transition fx-hooks intaking --workdir run
booping playbook-transition fx-hooks noted --workdir run
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
created index.md
not-started → intaking
frontmatter: status=intaking
intaking → noted
frontmatter: status=noted
script env-note: ok
-- stderr --
-- expected/cwd/run/env.txt --
artifact={CWD}/run/index.md
instance=
workdir={CWD}/run
cwd={CWD}/run
